 * Text to Speech tool (#1066, Epic #1064). Fetches the org's personal +
 * org-shared voice samples (`GET /api/v1/studio/voice-samples` via
 * `useVoiceSamples`) and lets the user pick one, writing the choice back to
 * the host via `onSelect`.
 *
 * The `studio.voice_samples` table ships empty until a future upload
 * ticket lands (Epic #1064 decision) — the empty state is a first-class,
 * expected state (AC: "If no voice samples exist for Qwen3-TTS, selector
 * shows empty state with a link to Settings > Voice Samples"), not a
 * placeholder. The link resolves to the real Coming-Soon placeholder route
 * already wired in `StudioApp.tsx` at `settings/voice-samples`.
 *
 * A `<fieldset>` + `<legend>` wraps every state (loading/error/empty/ready)
 * so the group has one stable accessible name throughout — mirrors the
 * fieldset/legend a11y convention used elsewhere in this MFE's forms
 * (real `<label>`/`aria-describedby`, §7 of the hard a11y rules).
 *
 * An "Upload new" affordance sits inside the same fieldset, below every
 * state (#1065-1070, step 11): it layers `VoiceSampleUploadModal` on top of
 * the host tool without navigating away or unmounting anything. On a
 * successful upload it closes the modal, auto-selects the new sample via
 * `onSelect`, and calls `useVoiceSamples`'s `retry()` to refetch the list —
 * the modal's own success Toast is the only user-facing confirmation, so
 * this component does not show a second one.
 *
 * Empty and error states each carry a real "Upload a sample" action (same
 * modal, via `setUploadOpen(true)`) alongside their existing secondary
 * action, per design.md sections 06-08's "two real next steps" and
 * "don't leave a dead end on failure" guidance — this component has a
 * single flat list (no Library/Documents tabs like the design board's
 * source composition), so the fix stays scoped to what actually exists
 * here: honest, non-overstated copy plus a working way forward.
 *
 * No audition/"Hear sample" affordance on the ready/chosen row: `VoiceSample`
 * (the list shape returned by `GET /voice-samples`) carries no playable URL
 * or `filesDocumentId` — only the create-response shape does — and no
 * `Hear sample` component exists elsewhere in this MFE to reuse. Adding one
 * here would mean inventing playback plumbing nobody asked for; tracked
 * separately rather than improvised in this pass.
 *
 * Delete (soft, via `DELETE /api/v1/studio/voice-samples/{id}`) is offered
 * ONLY in the expanded radiogroup, next to each sample the caller OWNS —
 * mirrors `VoiceSamplesSettingsRoute`'s rule that "can see it" (an org_shared
 * sample owned by someone else) must not imply "can delete it" (the svc
 * returns NOT_FOUND for a non-owner). Goes through the same AlertDialog
 * confirm pattern as the settings page. If the deleted sample was the one
 * currently selected, `onSelect("")` clears it — otherwise Generate would
 * stay enabled against a selection that can no longer resolve, and the job
 * would only fail once it reached the worker.
 *
 * cog-* tokens only (auto-adapt to dark mode via CSS variables).
